       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is above the usual maximum dose of 10 mg per day for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little blood pressure control.\n\nCould you check which of these you meant?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, which is the standard maximum dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, a typical starting dose. Some patients need less, such as frail or elderly patients, or those with hepatic impairment.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily**, if the dose is intentional. I can enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it, if you tell me the rationale.\n\nIf more blood pressure control is needed, adding another agent is usually preferred over going above 10 mg. Examples are an ACE inhibitor or ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
